 "sample_size_caveat": "Twenty gauges on twenty distinct river systems establish that the signal is not an artefact of one basin. They are NOT twenty independent tests of ENSO. They share one regional climate, so the independent dimension is the 76 winters, not the 20 gauges. Quote it as one region measured over 76 winters across twenty hydrologically distinct catchments, and do not multiply the two.",
 "what_this_does_not_show": "This measures peak daily mean DISCHARGE, not flooding. A river can rise a long way without leaving its channel, and none of these gauges has been compared against its NWS flood stage here. So the honest claim is that El Nino winters run higher on Florida's unregulated rivers, not that they flood more often. Establishing the second needs flood-stage thresholds per gauge and is a separate piece of work.",
